abstract: "This collection contains records that describe data (temperature, conductivity,\
  \ dissolved oxygen, fluorescence, photosynthetic active radiation, turbidity and\
  \ coloured dissolved organic matter) collected from vertical water property profiles.\
  \ These data were collected from ship-based casts and autonomous profilers by the\
  \ Hakai Institute from 2012 to present in waters surrounding Calvert Island, Johnstone\
  \ Strait, and Quadra Island areas. Users are encouraged to navigate to the individual\
  \ records holding their data of interest, or request specific data using the Data\
  \ Access Request Form.\n\nSpecifically, this collection includes CTD datasets made\
  \ by oceanographic profiler instruments (RBR XR-620, RBR Concerto, RBR Maestro,\
  \ and Seabird SBE 19plus v2) which have been automatically processed by following\
  \ respective manufacturer\u2019s guidelines. Both the provisional (no manual QC)\
  \ and the research-ready dataset are made available. The research-ready dataset\
  \ provides a subset of the provisional dataset which have been quality controlled\
  \ by applying a series of tests that are following the QARTOD standards and more\
  \ tests specific to the Hakai Institute (see Hakai Water Properties Profile Processing\
  \ and QA/QC Procedure Manual). The research-ready data are judged good for science\
  \ quality level.\n\nFurther, two versions of a dataset from a C-PROOF (Canadian\
  \ Pacific Robotic Ocean Observing Facility) Wirewalker are made available. The Wirewalker\
  \ is a wave-powered profiler moored in Bute Inlet, a fjord on the British Columbia\
  \ coast. The two versions include provisional data offloaded directly from the instrument,\
  \ which is the more complete dataset, and real-time data received via a satellite,\
  \ which is the more current dataset.\n\nData were collected by the Hakai Institute\
  \ Oceanography Program, the Nearshore Program, and the Juvenile Salmon Program."
