- description: 'Hakai Water Properties Profile Processing and QA/QC Procedure Manual
    (March 31, 2021): Procedure manual (version 1.0, March 2021) for processing and
    quality-controlling vertical ocean profile data, such as temperature, salinity,
    dissolved oxygen, turbidity, and light. It describes how CTD instruments from
    RBR and Seabird are deployed in the field and how their raw data are uploaded
    and matched with field metadata. It then lists the automated processing steps
    for each instrument type, which produce a consistent dataset averaged into 1-decibar
    depth bins. Quality control follows the QARTOD flagging standard, plus custom
    tests for problems like bottom hits, capped oxygen sensors, and boat shadow on
    light readings. The data are released in two versions: a provisional dataset with
    automated flags and a research dataset containing only manually reviewed, good-quality
    data.'
  type: url
  value: https://github.com/HakaiInstitute/hakai-erddap/blob/master/datasets_documents/HakaiWaterPropertiesProfiles/Hakai_Water_Properties_Processing_and_QAQC_Procedure_20210331.pdf
